# GrabMate — AI-Driven Multimodal Journey Recommendation

**A student-led product innovation and applied AI project | Ho Chi Minh City, 2025**  
**My role:** Project Leader · Project Manager · Lead MVP Developer  
**Team:** 6 members · **Approach:** CPMAI × Agile · **Project plan:** 10 weeks / 4 development sprints

![GrabMate project cover](assets/grabmate-cover.png)

> **Portfolio / academic project disclaimer:** GrabMate is a proposed concept developed for a university AI project. It is **not an official Grab product**, endorsed Grab integration, or live public-transit deployment. Some operations, rollout, and financial items in the coursework are plans or modeled scenarios, **not observed production outcomes**.

## At a glance

| Focus | Evidence / deliverable |
| --- | --- |
| Urban mobility & problem solving | First-mile/last-mile journey problem; integrated Grab + Bus / Metro options |
| Data & analytics | 500 sample multimodal trips, 50 columns in model source; traffic and route exploration |
| Machine learning | RandomForest_Deep for **recommended trip cost**; **R² 0.931**, **MAE 495.68 VND**, **MAPE 6.74%** on the notebook's held-out evaluation |
| MVP | Python notebook-based interactive journey recommendation demo using OSM/Nominatim geocoding, model-assisted fares and rule-based travel times |
| Leadership & project management | WBS, ownership matrix, four-sprint delivery plan, communication plan, risk register, launch OKRs and closeout document |
| Product / business case | Problem framing, prototype, financial assumptions and proposed Go-to-Market / operationalization |

**Important metric distinction:** The trained ML target is `recommended_total_cost_vnd` (trip **cost**, not ETA). The MVP's travel-time estimates are based on distance/transport assumptions. Dataset/test metrics are **offline prototype evidence**, not real-world travel-time improvements. Earlier draft values such as ETA R²≈0.588 should **not** be used as results for this notebook.

## 1. Problem & opportunity

Travelers combining ride-hailing with bus or metro encounter disconnected planning, uncertain transfers and first-/last-mile friction. GrabMate explores an **end-to-end route comparison** of ride-hailing-only and public-transit-supported alternatives, helping a commuter balance **estimated fare**, **time**, and **route availability**. The target scenarios cover the Metro Line 1 corridor and connecting bus access across Ho Chi Minh City.

**Core question:** How might a mobility platform make GrabBike/GrabCar + Bus/Metro trips easier to compare and plan, without assuming an existing production integration?

## 2. Product concept & MVP flow

1. Enter origin and destination (the demo includes selected UEH location aliases).
2. Resolve locations through a local alias mapping or OpenStreetMap Nominatim.
3. Generate candidate modes: Grab only, Grab → Bus and Grab → Metro where supported.
4. Estimate distance, journey duration and transport fares; use the trained ML model for cost estimation where available, with rule-based fallback.
5. Compare options and recommend a route using the prototype's selection logic.
6. Display transfer/stop details where data is defined.

The demo uses **simulated traffic states** and simplified fares/times, not live Grab booking, verified real-time bus arrival feeds, or production navigation.

**Demo:** [Watch the included walkthrough](prototype/GrabMate_Demo.mp4) · [Original project landing page](https://bit.ly/486Xamc) · [Original project Notion](https://bit.ly/3KqCV9T)

